    "pressure": {
        "_doc": "Pressure clocks (src/systems/pressure.js): the world answers a mighty House on a cadence that follows its power, not on rare rolls. might = (power score - floor) / (full - floor), clamped 0..1, from the weekly Coalitions.power reckoning (older than staleDays counts as 0). A clock winds by days / interval, the interval running from slowDays at minMight down to fastDays at might 1; below minMight it drains. It fires at 1 +/- jitter (a hash, no RNG). coalition: when ripe, for primedDays realms swear a league at joinShare x joinAt hostility even below formAt (paused while a league stands or in its cooldown). siege: weekly (cadence) while the player holds a colony or own-name town; when ripe the most hostile, nearest realm (hostility >= minHostility, or already at war) sends a host straight at a holding, or demands tribute and marches if refused (pendingDays); cooldownDays follow. heat: each firing adds 1 (to max), dividing the next interval by 1 + step x heat; it cools decayPerYear and an heir keeps heirKeep of it (escalation across a reign, capped for century-long games). Tuned for decades (120 days a year). saga: gap between sagas x lerp(gapMult[weak], gapMult[strong]), repeatAfterDays x lerp(repeatMult), +1 maxActive at extraActiveAt, and past hookAt word of a new saga is brought to the player's court.",
